{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966806,"nonce":"fHUZLOHZecdHH0HHk0as4ynrQ5Q=","title":"Div::on_unmount handlers never run in a real app; the live unmount signal is the stable-id","message":"`event_types::UNMOUNT` is emitted from exactly one place,\n`EventRouter::on_unmount`, which is reached from exactly one place,\n`EventRouter::diff_trees`, which is called only from its own unit\ntests. So `Div::on_unmount` / `Stateful::on_unmount` compile, register,\nand never fire in a running app.\n\n`diff_trees` is also unsound as written: it diffs sets of\n`LayoutNodeId`, and those are slotmap keys that recycle across\nrebuilds. A recycled id reads as still-mounted, and an id kept across a\nrebuild never reads as unmounted. See\n[[gotcha-stale-subtree-rebuild-across-builds]].\n\n**Where the real signal is.** `RenderTree::mint_stable_ids_walk` re-mints\na `StableNodeId` for every live node from the root on every rebuild\npath (full build, subtree rebuild, diff), so right after it\n`stable_to_layout.keys()` IS the live set. `sweep_stale_handlers` and\n`sweep_stale_css_animations` already turn that into \"what did not\nsurvive this build\" and evict. Anything that needs unmount should be a\nthird sweep next to those two, keyed on `StableNodeId`, not a listener\non the dead UNMOUNT event.\n\nWatch the call sites: the two sweeps are paired on the subtree and diff\npaths, but the full-build path calls only `sweep_stale_handlers`. A new\nsweep has to be added to every rebuild path deliberately, and a path\nthat mints without sweeping leaks rather than mis-evicting.\n\n**Why it matters:** unmount is the one lifetime fact Zyntax's uses-graph\ncannot infer, so Blinc has to report it — see\n[[feedback-dont-reinvent-the-runtime]] and\n[[project-signals-are-effect-handles]]. Reporting it from a hook that\nnever fires would look wired and free nothing.","files":null}]}